re КП rolling scheme. КП+УО sheet rolling duration is shorter by 150 s compared with it, and the relationship identifies row low-temperature КП as the comparison scheme for the 150 s shorter duration. [Data: Entities (1681, 1700); Relationships (3463, 3460)]\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Finishing-stand rolling is the operational stage where the duration benefit appears\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Sheet rolling in the finishing stand is the specific operation whose duration is shorter for КП+УО, by 50 s or more than 1.5 times compared with КП+УО+КП and by 150 s compared with row low-temperature КП. The relationship also states that sheet rolling occurs in the finishing stand. This focuses the productivity impact on the finishing mill rather than upstream stages. [Data: Entities (1684); Relationships (3453, 3412)]\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Temperature increase is a key trade-off affecting hold time and productivity\",\n      \"explanation\": \"КП+УО uses finishing-stand temperatures 30–50 °C higher than ordinary controlled rolling, and this temperature increase affects hold time and mill productivity. The scheme is therefore not only a cooling innovation but also a temperature-regime choice that changes timing and throughput in the rolling process. [Data: Entities (1565, 1668); Relationships (3202)]\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}, "metrics": {"attempted_request_count": 1, "successful_response_count": 0, "failed_response_count": 0, "responses_with_tokens": 1, "prompt_tokens": 4264, "completion_tokens": 6173, "total_tokens": 10437, "compute_duration_seconds": 28.859658002853394, "streaming_responses": 0, "retries": 0, "requests_with_retries": 0}}}